WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.880
<v Narrator><i>Sing now: the Greeks' emergence, the sack, and Odysseus's attack on Deiphobus's house.</i>

2
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:18.810
<v Narrator><i>Odysseus weeps like a captive woman over a fallen husband.</i>

3
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:49.700
<v Alcinous>Stop the lyre, Demodocus — not all here take joy of it, for since the song began our guest has not once left off weeping. Now, stranger, hide it no longer: tell me the name your father and mother called you, and your land and your city. And say why you weep at the doom of the Argives and Troy — did some kinsman fall there, or a comrade dear as a brother?

4
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:56.270
<v Narrator><i>Odysseus prepares to narrate his wanderings.</i>
